      "tests": "cargo test -p e3-zk-prover (in-module tests and src/*_tests.rs). Integration: cargo test -p e3-zk-prover --features integration-tests (tests/integration_tests.rs). build.rs runs scripts/build_fixtures.sh unless E3_ZK_PROVER_SKIP_FIXTURE_BUILD=1 (build.rs:25). Tests marked #[ignore] need prepared artifacts; their message names pnpm rust:test:proofs.",
      "unverified": [
        "DkgAggregator and DecryptionAggregator witnesses are built from the Default-variant circuit JSON (node_dkg_fold.rs:528 and :592) and proved with the Evm target (:536 and :665); I did not confirm that the default and evm circuit JSON files are identical.",
        "NodeProofAggregator publishes DKGRecursiveAggregationComplete without a proof when proof_aggregation_enabled is false (node_proof_aggregation/effects.rs:25-31); its log calls this test-only. I did not trace where the flag is set.",
        "versions.json circuits_checksums lists only 0.18.0 while required_circuits_version is 0.19.0; the 0.19.0 digest is inserted at build time from E3_CIRCUITS_ARCHIVE_SHA256 (config.rs:80-85). I did not check how release builds set that variable.",
        "NodeProofAggregator persists through e3-data Repositories (node_proof_aggregation/actor.rs:45); whether that store is sled-backed was not traced (crates/data/src/lib.rs:18 declares sled_db).",
        "The commitment_links/*.rs consistency rules and the ECDSA checks in share_verification/transitions/ecdsa.rs were not read beyond their names.",
        "The TaskPool, retry and memory logic in crates/multithread was not read beyond the dispatch path."
      ]
